# 10. SMART TRAILING STOP ENGINE

Implement multiple trailing-stop methods.

## A. ATR Trailing

Trail behind eligible market price using a configured ATR multiple.

## B. Structural Trailing

Use newly confirmed swing highs/lows.

For BUY:
- Trail below confirmed higher lows.

For SELL:
- Trail above confirmed lower highs.

## C. Candle-Based Trailing

Use confirmed candle structure under defined rules.

## D. Momentum Trailing

Adapt trailing behavior based on Phase 2 momentum state within the selected policy.

## E. Hybrid Trailing

Use structure and volatility together.

## Critical requirements

A protective trailing stop must never loosen simply because volatility increases later, unless an explicitly different management model permits and records that behavior.

For normal protective trailing:

- BUY stop must not move downward.
- SELL stop must not move upward.

Implement stop ratcheting and tick-size rounding.

Only move stops when the required information becomes available.

Prevent historical repainting.

Do not create unrealistically perfect trailing exits using future candle highs/lows.

